  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Shade-grown Cocoa Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central Africa Regional):  USAID&apos;s Shade-grown Cocoa Activity will establish employment opportunities for local populations, sound management of primary and secondary forests, and decrease deforestation pressure for extractive uses of forests. The activity will 1) establish and strengthen networks of cocoa producers to improve the quality, quantity and sustainability of their cocoa; 2) establish and strengthen linkages with all stages in the cocoa value chain as a sustainable, forest-friendly export crop; 3) strengthen enabling conditions needed for the success of the cocoa value chain; and 4) increase revenue and non-revenue benefits of stakeholder farmers. USAID intends to leverage, at a minimum, matching funds from the private sector. While the &quot;focused&quot; Sustainable Landscape funds will be used primarily to alleviate the pressure of deforestation, they will indirectly contribute to biodiversity outcomes by protecting forest habitat and key biodiversity species in these important forests. By demonstrating an effective approach to reducing deforestation, they will also assist the government of the Democratic Republic of the Congo to meet its Nationally Determined Contribution under the Paris Climate Agreement..This activity will contribute to advancing U.S. government priorities in Central Africa designed to maintain the ecological integrity of the humid forest ecosystem of the Congo Basin, which is vital to regional stability, a U.S. foreign policy priority. It contributes to Joint Strategic Plan Strategic Objective 2.2: (Promote healthy, educated and productive populations in partner countries to drive inclusive and sustainable development, open new markets and support U.S. prosperity and security objectives) by protecting natural resources critical to long term, sustainable growth, and food and water security. This activity will support the implementation of USAID&apos;s Private Sector Engagement Strategy as well as the Climate Strategy... .</narrative>
  </description>
